Description: pco: clamp texel buffer indices to the number of elements
 A texel buffer view is a linear 2D texture 8192 texels wide with
 DIV_ROUND_UP(elements, 8192) rows (pvr_CreateBufferView()), and pco
 turns the element index into (index % 8192, index / 8192) for texel
 fetches and for storage texel buffer access. The texture unit only checks
 against that 2D extent, so an index past the last element but inside the
 last row reads or writes up to 8191 elements beyond the buffer, which
 faults when the next page is unmapped. Helper invocations at the edge of
 a draw produce such indices, for example in the st/mesa PBO upload shader.
 Without robust buffer access, clamp the index to the last element
 (PCO_IMAGE_META_BUFFER_ELEMS). With it, send an index past the last
 element to row 16383, outside every view, so the texture unit handles it
 like any other out of bounds coordinate instead of reading past the buffer.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
